. LESSON 6 DEBUGGING
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. The lesson's mistakes, each with its fix, which runs:
.
. POINT 14;30,4 has a semicolon where a comma goes.
POINT 14,30,4
. SKIP-2 needs a space, SKIP -2, or it subtracts 2 from SKIP.
. POINT (14,30,2) has a space before its parenthesis.
POINT(14,30,2)
. TEST="PRINT '"'" puts a quote inside quotes. Brackets nest, quotes
. don't, so:
TEST=[PRINT '"']
TEST
. IF A=10,PRINT "huh?" always prints, because = sets A to 10. Use ==
IF A==10,PRINT "huh?"
.
. Reckless abbreviation: in DOODLE CR1,CR2,...,CR10,CR11, CR1 could be
. CR10 or CR11 too. Name them CR01, CR02 and so on.
. SIN FIRST,ORIGINAL can't make a macro SIN, which is a system function.
.
. The lesson's advice: put a PRINT in a loop to watch a variable change.
. The animation does, printing M each pass. Watch it in fullscreen.

. THE ANIMATION. TIMES draws the times table of M around a circle:
. a line from each of 60 points, N, to point N*M. M grows a little each
. pass, so the figure turns from a heart to a kidney to a flower. The
. lines are drawn in XOR, colormodes 5 to 7. The first pass just draws
. them. After that each step draws a line to N*M and then the last
. pass's line to N*MO again, which takes it off, so nothing is ever
. cleared. Where lines cross, their colors mix.
. The node's Stop button stops it, and Play carries on.
TIMES=[CLEAR;N=0;M=2
LINE 115*COS(N*6),96*SIN(N*6),4;LINE 115*COS(N*M*6),96*SIN(N*M*6),N\3+5
IF (N=N+1)<60,SKIP -1
P=0
1PASS P=P+1;N=0;M=(200+4*P)/100;MO=(200+4*(P-1))/100;PRINT M
1LINE A=N*6;B=N*M*6;C=N*MO*6;K=N\3+5;LINE 115*COS(A),96*SIN(A),4;LINE 115*COS(B),96*SIN(B),K;LINE 115*COS(A),96*SIN(A),4;LINE 115*COS(C),96*SIN(C),K
IF (N=N+1)<60,GOTO 1LINE
GOTO 1PASS]
TIMES
